Part 1

2
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:01,623
Man:

3
00:00:01,623 --> 00:00:01,884
Hello.

4
00:00:01,884 --> 00:00:06,207
Do you mind if I ask you some questions about your journey today?

5
00:00:06,207 --> 00:00:08,290
We're doing a customer satisfaction survey.

6
00:00:08,290 --> 00:00:08,618
Sophie:

7
00:00:08,618 --> 00:00:08,946
Yes.

8
00:00:08,946 --> 00:00:09,273
OK.

9
00:00:09,273 --> 00:00:12,551
I've got about ten minutes before my train home leaves.

10
00:00:12,551 --> 00:00:14,190
I'm on a day trip.

11
00:00:14,190 --> 00:00:14,514
Man:

12
00:00:14,514 --> 00:00:14,839
Great.

13
00:00:14,839 --> 00:00:15,487
Thank you.

14
00:00:15,487 --> 00:00:18,730
So first of all, could you tell me your name?

15
00:00:18,730 --> 00:00:19,225
Sophie:

16
00:00:19,225 --> 00:00:20,710
It's Sophie Bird.

17
00:00:20,710 --> 00:00:21,022
Man:

18
00:00:21,022 --> 00:00:21,648
Thank you.

19
00:00:21,648 --> 00:00:24,460
And would you mind telling me what you do?

20
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:24,822
Sophie:

21
00:00:24,822 --> 00:00:25,910
I'm a journalist.

22
00:00:25,910 --> 00:00:26,237
Man:

23
00:00:26,237 --> 00:00:26,891
Oh really?

24
00:00:26,891 --> 00:00:28,200
That must be interesting.

25
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:28,540
Sophie:

26
00:00:28,540 --> 00:00:28,880
Yes.

27
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:29,560
It is.

28
00:00:29,560 --> 00:00:29,906
Man:

29
00:00:29,906 --> 00:00:33,370
So was the reason for your visit here today work?

30
00:00:33,370 --> 00:00:33,675
Sophie:

31
00:00:33,675 --> 00:00:35,198
Actually, it's my day off.

32
00:00:35,198 --> 00:00:37,330
I came here to do some shopping.

33
00:00:37,330 --> 00:00:37,687
Man:

34
00:00:37,687 --> 00:00:38,400
Oh right.

35
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:38,697
Sophie:

36
00:00:38,697 --> 00:00:41,070
But I do sometimes come here for work.

37
00:00:41,070 --> 00:00:41,400
Man:

38
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:41,730
OK.

39
00:00:41,730 --> 00:00:46,350
Now I'd like to ask some questions about your journey today, if that's OK.

40
00:00:46,350 --> 00:00:46,658
Sophie:

41
00:00:46,658 --> 00:00:46,965
Yes.

42
00:00:46,965 --> 00:00:47,580
No problem.

43
00:00:47,580 --> 00:00:47,920
Man:

44
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:48,260
Right,

45
00:00:48,260 --> 00:00:52,000
so can you tell me which station you're travelling back to?

46
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:52,472
Sophie:

47
00:00:52,472 --> 00:00:54,360
Staunfirth, where I live.

48
00:00:54,360 --> 00:00:55,571
Man:

49
00:00:55,571 --> 00:01:02,839
Can I just check the spelling?

50
00:01:02,839 --> 00:01:04,050
S-T-A-U-N-F-I-R-T-H?

51
00:01:04,050 --> 00:01:04,297
Sophie:

52
00:01:04,297 --> 00:01:04,790
That's right.

53
00:01:04,790 --> 00:01:05,244
Man:

54
00:01:05,244 --> 00:01:08,420
And you travelled from there this morning?

55
00:01:08,420 --> 00:01:08,870
Sophie:

56
00:01:08,870 --> 00:01:09,320
Yes.

57
00:01:09,320 --> 00:01:09,640
Man:

58
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:10,281
OK, good.

59
00:01:10,281 --> 00:01:13,485
Next, can I ask what kind of ticket you bought?

60
00:01:13,485 --> 00:01:17,650
I assume it wasn't a season ticket, as you don't travel every day.

61
00:01:17,650 --> 00:01:18,018
Sophie:

62
00:01:18,018 --> 00:01:18,755
That's right.

63
00:01:18,755 --> 00:01:21,701
No, I just got a normal return ticket.

64
00:01:21,701 --> 00:01:26,120
I don't have a rail card so I didn't get any discount.

65
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:29,080
I keep meaning to get one because it's a lot cheaper.

66
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:29,435
Man:

67
00:01:29,435 --> 00:01:32,627
Yes – you'd have saved 20% on your ticket today.

68
00:01:32,627 --> 00:01:35,820
So you paid the full price for your ticket?

69
00:01:35,820 --> 00:01:36,310
Sophie:

70
00:01:36,310 --> 00:01:38,270
I paid ￡23.70.

71
00:01:38,270 --> 00:01:38,562
Man:

72
00:01:38,562 --> 00:01:38,854
OK.

73
00:01:38,854 --> 00:01:41,190
Do you think that's good value for money?

74
00:01:41,190 --> 00:01:41,472
Sophie:

75
00:01:41,472 --> 00:01:42,038
Not really.

76
00:01:42,038 --> 00:01:45,710
I think it's too much for a journey that only takes 45 minutes.

77
00:01:45,710 --> 00:01:46,027
Man:

78
00:01:46,027 --> 00:01:46,344
Yes,

79
00:01:46,344 --> 00:01:48,882
that's one of the main complaints we get.

80
00:01:48,882 --> 00:01:51,420
So, you didn't buy your ticket in advance?

81
00:01:51,420 --> 00:01:51,672
Sophie:

82
00:01:51,672 --> 00:01:51,924
No.

83
00:01:51,924 --> 00:01:54,695
I know it's cheaper if you buy a week in advance

84
00:01:54,695 --> 00:01:56,710
but I didn't know I was coming then.

85
00:01:56,710 --> 00:01:57,086
Man:

86
00:01:57,086 --> 00:01:57,838
I know.

87
00:01:57,838 --> 00:01:59,718
You can't always plan ahead.

88
00:01:59,718 --> 00:02:02,350
So, did you buy it this morning?

89
00:02:02,350 --> 00:02:02,780
Sophie:

90
00:02:02,780 --> 00:02:04,500
No, it was yesterday.

91
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:04,849
Man:

92
00:02:04,849 --> 00:02:05,198
Right.

93
00:02:05,198 --> 00:02:08,690
And do you usually buy your tickets at the station?

94
00:02:08,690 --> 00:02:09,055
Sophie:

95
00:02:09,055 --> 00:02:12,702
Well, I do usually but the ticket office closes early

96
00:02:12,702 --> 00:02:14,890
and I hate using ticket machines.

97
00:02:14,890 --> 00:02:17,764
I think ticket offices should be open for longer hours.

98
00:02:17,764 --> 00:02:21,500
There's always a queue for the machines and they're often out of order.

99
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:21,783
Man:

100
00:02:21,783 --> 00:02:24,330
A lot of customers are saying the same thing.

101
00:02:24,330 --> 00:02:24,777
Sophie:

102
00:02:24,777 --> 00:02:29,250
So to answer your question … I got an e-ticket online.

103
00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:29,622
Man:

104
00:02:29,622 --> 00:02:29,994
OK.

105
00:02:29,994 --> 00:02:30,739
Thank you.

106
00:02:30,739 --> 00:02:35,206
Now I'd like to ask you about your satisfaction with your journey.

107
00:02:35,206 --> 00:02:39,300
So what would you say you were most satisfied with today?

108
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:39,624
Sophie:

109
00:02:39,624 --> 00:02:42,216
Well, I like the wifi on the train.

110
00:02:42,216 --> 00:02:43,512
It's improved a lot.

111
00:02:43,512 --> 00:02:47,400
It makes it easier for me to work if I want to.

112
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:47,686
Man:

113
00:02:47,686 --> 00:02:49,975
That's the first time today anyone's mentioned that.

114
00:02:49,975 --> 00:02:52,550
It's good to get some positive feedback on that.

115
00:02:52,550 --> 00:02:52,945
Sophie:

116
00:02:52,945 --> 00:02:53,340
Mmm.

117
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:53,794
Man:

118
00:02:53,794 --> 00:02:57,430
And, is there anything you weren't satisfied with?

119
00:02:57,430 --> 00:02:57,840
Sophie:

120
00:02:57,840 --> 00:03:02,350
Well, normally, the trains run on time and are pretty reliable

121
00:03:02,350 --> 00:03:04,810
but today there was a delay;

122
00:03:04,810 --> 00:03:08,090
the train was about 15 minutes behind schedule.

123
00:03:08,090 --> 00:03:08,474
Man:

124
00:03:08,474 --> 00:03:08,859
OK.

125
00:03:08,859 --> 00:03:10,397
I'll put that down.

126
00:03:10,397 --> 00:03:15,010
Now I'd also like to ask about the facilities at this station.

127
00:03:15,010 --> 00:03:18,976
You've probably noticed that the whole station's been upgraded.

128
00:03:18,976 --> 00:03:21,620
What are you most satisfied with?

129
00:03:21,620 --> 00:03:22,007
Sophie:

130
00:03:22,007 --> 00:03:27,422
I think the best thing is that they've improved the amount of information about

131
00:03:27,422 --> 00:03:28,583
train times etc.

132
00:03:28,583 --> 00:03:30,130
that's given to passengers.

133
00:03:30,130 --> 00:03:33,574
– it's much clearer – before there was only one board

134
00:03:33,574 --> 00:03:37,400
and I couldn't always see it properly – which was frustrating.

135
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:37,767
Man:

136
00:03:37,767 --> 00:03:38,502
That's good.

137
00:03:38,502 --> 00:03:41,440
And is there anything you're not satisfied with?

138
00:03:41,440 --> 00:03:41,856
Sophie:

139
00:03:41,856 --> 00:03:46,012
Let's see … I think things have generally improved a lot.

140
00:03:46,012 --> 00:03:51,000
The trains are much more modern and I like the new café.

141
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:55,935
But one thing is that there aren't enough places to sit down, especially on

142
00:03:55,935 --> 00:03:56,640
the platforms.

143
00:03:56,640 --> 00:03:56,989
Man:

144
00:03:56,989 --> 00:04:01,531
OK – so I'll put 'seating' down, shall I, as the thing you're least

145
00:04:01,531 --> 00:04:02,230
satisfied with?

146
00:04:02,230 --> 00:04:02,777
Sophie:

147
00:04:02,777 --> 00:04:03,323
Yes.

148
00:04:03,323 --> 00:04:03,870
OK.

149
00:04:03,870 --> 00:04:04,302
Man:

150
00:04:04,302 --> 00:04:09,048
Can I ask your opinion about some of the other facilities?

151
00:04:09,048 --> 00:04:15,090
We'd like feedback on whether people are satisfied, dissatisfied or neither satisfied nor dissatisfied.

152
00:04:15,090 --> 00:04:15,675
Sophie:

153
00:04:15,675 --> 00:04:16,260
OK.

154
00:04:16,260 --> 00:04:16,665
Man:

155
00:04:16,665 --> 00:04:19,500
What about the parking at the station?

156
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:19,791
Sophie:

157
00:04:19,791 --> 00:04:23,869
Well to be honest, I don't really have an opinion as I never use

158
00:04:23,869 --> 00:04:24,160
it.

159
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:24,571
Man:

160
00:04:24,571 --> 00:04:27,860
So, neither satisfied nor dissatisfied for that then.

161
00:04:27,860 --> 00:04:28,330
Sophie:

162
00:04:28,330 --> 00:04:30,210
Yes, I suppose so …

163
00:04:30,210 --> 00:04:30,368
Man:

164
00:04:30,368 --> 00:04:30,526
OK,

165
00:04:30,526 --> 00:04:31,000
and what about …?
